# Auto-push after changes

When you modify files in this repository, **commit and push to git before ending your turn**, unless the user explicitly says not to.

## Protocol

1. After completing code changes, run in parallel:
   - `git status`
   - `git diff` (staged and unstaged)
   - `git log -1 --oneline` (match commit message style)
2. Stage relevant files with `git add` (never `.env`, credentials, or gitignored runtime logs).
3. Commit with a concise message focused on **why**.
4. Push: `git push origin HEAD`
5. Confirm clean sync with `git status`.

## Safety

- NEVER update git config
- NEVER force-push to main/master
- NEVER commit secrets (`.env`, API keys)
- NEVER skip hooks
- If push fails (offline/auth), report the error; do not force-push

## Also runs automatically

- Cursor `stop` hook: `.cursor/hooks/auto-push.sh`
- Git `post-commit` hook (after local commits): run `bash scripts/install-auto-push.sh` once per machine
